    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": false,
        "readOnlyHint": true,
      },
      "description": "Find context items and definitions by words, or list them by kind or domain. Use it to look names up, to browse or to pick some, never to answer a question about a metric, dimension values and dates (call get_context). With words, it finds what is written down by the names people use: metrics and their other names (such as GMV), dimension values (such as Norway), domains, member names from the data tool (such as payments.orders), and words in an item's title, summary or text. Use it for "what do we know about", "what is" or "how is it defined", and when you don't know the exact names. It returns the matching items, each with its title and summary, and for each metric or dimension the words name, the definition its source gives and what this context adds. When no words match, it returns the items that apply to what the words name, on the dates the window or the words give, or else today, as say says; when nothing is found, why says what to try. Without words, it lists everything there is of a kind or in a domain, in a fixed order: definitions first, metrics, dimensions and terms, each A to Z with a one-line meaning, then items A to Z by title, each with its summary. Filter by kind (metric, dimension, term, event, warning, rule or guide) and domain (a name such as Sales). Every reply says how many there are; pass next_cursor as cursor for the next page. terms gives each word of the query a person defined in Definitions, with its meaning as written. No row carries an item's text: read one in full with read_context.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
