      "description": "One context item or one definition in full, with its links. Read one by an id or a name another reply gave. An item comes with its text, its sources with the sentence each one gives, who checked it and when, its not_to_conclude line, and terms, each word of it a person defined in Definitions, with its meaning as written; then links_out, what it links to, and links_in, a page of the items that link to it, each with how it links (relations keeps only those kinds). Read a linked item the same way to follow a link, only when it helps answer the question: a link neither widens where an item applies nor proves a cause. A definition, by its name, another of its names or its key from find_context, is for when the person asks what something means or how it is defined: its words whole, as its source or a person wrote them, where they come from, its owner as a role, its other names, its family with what the family means and its usual metric, what it is built from, and the titles of the published items about it, even when there are none; never to answer a question about the data, which get_context does. An edition needs a service token with edition scope.",
