      "description": "Send a draft of the person's own to the owner, after the person says yes. Call it only after the person says yes to sending it. Pass the draft_id that write_draft gave and the revision the person saw: it sends exactly that revision, as the signed-in person, to the owner of its domain, who checks it and publishes it: nothing changes until they do. The one exception is an owner who lets this agent publish without review in their domain: a new low-risk item that clashes with nothing is then published at once, as their decision, and the reply says so. If the draft changed since that revision, nothing is sent and changed_since lists the fields: read it with read_draft, show the person, and ask again. If the review checks find a problem, it stays the person's draft and blocking says why. Tell the person what the reply says, that it waits for the owner or that it was published, and give them the link.",
